y rollback, no new temporary-file residue or listening services appeared, and package-health output was unchanged from baseline.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9960fca0ef134721","cmd-a4cfd8cf14094277","cmd-59a9f65a294f4424","cmd-214ceec8979147ee","cmd-43bd2aeea1c1458d","cmd-4d8ebf95eb5b443d","cmd-5cb6578abd0643ba","cmd-120e89c7ff0c4650","cmd-0d83565652ee44ee","cmd-c948725be70f49ef","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied with direct, coherent evidence. The snapshot captured known-good /srv/data state, subsequent divergence was observed, and rollback restored the earlier contents and relevant metadata. The provider-wide restart protocol for node1 is complete: it includes healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, a changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle observations, and recovered mount, services, data, and snapshot state.","limitations":["The lifecycle failed-services probe was unsupported because it checks systemd on Alpine; direct OpenRC checks nevertheless showed localmount and sshd healthy after restart.","The explicit exactness checks covered recursive file comparison, hashes, modes, symlink target, and unwanted-file absence; ownership, timestamps, ACLs, and extended attributes were not separately enumerated."]}
